// 004.11: a derivation rule says which status it means. An act's own `Holds when` and
// `Valid when` may still read the fact bare, and are then three-valued.
Fact person Identified by Walter
Evidenced Bool lacks-capacity
Bool questioned Holds when Not(Unresolved(lacks-capacity()))
Bool found-lacking Holds when Established(lacks-capacity())
Fact decided Identified by person
Power decide Actor person Holds when Not(lacks-capacity()) Valid when Not(lacks-capacity()) Creates decided()
Act determine Actor person Holds when True Supports lacks-capacity()
.
?!questioned(). ?!found-lacking().
?undetermined decide(Walter).
determine(Walter).
?questioned(). ?found-lacking().
?!valid decide(Walter).
